		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋφρ</span>-, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with kind</i> (or <i>prudent) mind</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ</span> (or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅς</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> σφιν ἐϋφρονέων ἀγορήσατο καὶ
					μετέειπεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.73
				</span></i>
			, al.; fem. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έουσα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.998
			</span></i>: pl. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έοντες</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Man.
				1.233
			</span></i>. (The Verb-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρονέω</span> is not
			found; perh. better divisim.)</div>
